// Rain on surfaces (RainSurface), to listen to rather than measure: a 25x25 stage of one material at y 244, over
// dark forest (no other scenario builds there), with the player standing on it, or under a roof of it at y 248 (vanilla
// plays its quieter, lower "rain above" sound on a roof over the player). Vanilla picks the block each rain sound plays on
// from columns within 10 blocks of the player's height, so up here every sound is on the stage: the ground is far below.
// Each stage twice, Rain on surfaces on and then off; the run's name shows in chat and over the hotbar as it starts,
// and its caption under the recording's line. The storm is held at 60% (calm and medium rain, a little heavy); the mod's
// ambient sounds and the music are turned off. The water stage is a pool with a stone rim at 13 blocks, past the columns
// sampled. Recordings are made but aren't the point.
// See README.md for the format.
